postreload: fold "r = r + C" into a following "r = @(r)"  [PR52049]

reload_combine folds a constant add into the addresses that use it.  It
stopped when the use also writes the register, as in "r1 = @(r1)", so
the last of several loads off one base kept a separate add (SH2):

    before:  add #12,r1 / mov.l @r1,r1
    after:   mov.l @(12,r1),r1

That insn overwrites the register, so it is the add's last use: once
the constant is in the address the add is dead and can be deleted, the
same way two adds in a row are already merged.

GCC 15 gets this from the new late_combine pass; this is the small
14.x equivalent.  Part of the SH addressing meta-bug PR56590.

Tested on sh-elf -m2 (GCC 14.2.0; postreload.cc is identical in 14.3.0):
gcc.c-torture/execute at -O1/-O2/-O3/-Os on the GDB SH simulator, 5500
passes before and after, no result changed; gcc.c-torture compile+execute
at -O2/-Os: no ICEs, .text unchanged at -O2, -8 bytes at -Os.

Backported to 12.4.0 (applies with line offsets), tested together with
the other SH patches on sh-elf -m2: gcc.c-torture/execute at
-O1/-O2/-O3/-Os on the GDB SH simulator, no result changed
(1446/1450/1451/1434 passes); gcc.c-torture compile+execute: no ICEs;
-O2 -g -fcompare-debug: no new failures.

gcc/ChangeLog:

	PR target/52049
	* postreload.cc (reload_combine_recognize_const_pattern): Also
	delete the add when the use is inside a MEM of an insn that
	overwrites the add's destination register.

--- a/gcc-12.4.0/gcc/postreload.cc
+++ b/gcc-12.4.0/gcc/postreload.cc
@@ -1008,10 +1008,15 @@
 	    break;
 
 	  /* We also must not move the addition past an insn that sets
-	     the same register, unless we can combine two add insns.  */
+	     the same register, unless we can combine two add insns, or
+	     the insn overwrites the whole register (e.g. "r1 = @(r1)"):
+	     then this is the last use and the add is dead once its
+	     constant is folded into the address.  */
 	  if (must_move_add && reg_state[regno].store_ruid == use_ruid)
 	    {
-	      if (use->containing_mem == NULL_RTX)
+	      rtx use_set = single_set (use_insn);
+	      if (use->containing_mem == NULL_RTX
+		  || (use_set && rtx_equal_p (SET_DEST (use_set), reg)))
 		delete_add = true;
 	      else
 		break;
